<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    v115 — Curio's cosmic launcher mark, applied from the designer's NEW
    SVG (svgviewer-output (5).svg, archived at
    design/launcher-icon/curio-launcher-icon-v2.svg) rendered to a 2048×2048
    raster (drawable-nodpi/ic_launcher_icon.png): a mint planet with a pink
    moon over layered pink/gold waves on a midnight navy→magenta sky, inside
    a rounded card. Same card geometry as the previous art (84–88% of the
    canvas) — only the white frame is gone, matching the new source.

    The art is a ROUNDED CARD with transparent corners — at the
    adaptive-icon canvas size (108dp) the card spans ~84–88%, which the
    launcher's mask (66dp safe zone) would crop: the frame, top stars and
    bottom waves were getting sliced ("broken / not properly placed"). So
    the bitmap is inset 18dp on every side: the art fills the central
    72dp, the card lands at ~60×63dp — still inside the safe circle (66dp)
    but much larger than the v115 28dp inset (~44×47dp), which read as a
    tiny "icon inside the icon" on the launcher. The card floats on the
    full-bleed sky in ic_launcher_background.xml (whose gradient matches
    the card's own sky, so the two composite seamlessly behind the card).
    The 2048px source downscales cleanly to every density.

    The SPLASH screen renders @drawable/ic_launcher_icon (the same new
    art) directly — the old bordered raster is gone (v126).
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:inset="18dp"
    android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_icon" />
